# Writing and remembering yaml filesG
 Always remember 4 things,
 
1. apiVersion

   -> Every k8s resource has a version. example, pods, services has v1 and sets like replicasest, deployment has apps/v1
   -> type kubectl api-resources to see the api versions

2. kind

   -> kind is nothing but which type of k8s resource that we need like Pod, Service, Replicaset etc
   -> Again, type kubectl api-resources to see the kinds

3. metadata

   -> metadata containes name of the kind, such as pod name, service name etc.. you can give names as you like.
   -> metadata also contains labels, uisng labels we can group all the resources like if service and pod contains same lables thyen service attaches pods to      its endpoints.

4. spec

   -> spec denotes what type of specification we need, like if we mention kind as replicaset, than we need 3 replicas and that we will mention in spec, alos      containers, we will mention contianer image name, conatiner name here.

